33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The roads closed, but the halls stayed open. That’s a good sign for local resilience.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The digitisation project failed. Half the images are unindexed. We shouldn't repeat that.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"We have volunteers, but no one to supervise them. That’s a critical gap.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,The grant only covers sessions for a year. Then we pay from the flat budget. That’s a trap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The bus links are gone. People can’t get to us easily. That’s a huge problem.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, if the grant ends, do we have to stop the service?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, likely. Unless we find a sustainable model. The old one didn't work.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the neighbourhood groups are self-sustaining. Maybe we should partner with them?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, that’s possible. But we need to check if they have the right skills.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, the remote use peaks after we close. We need to extend hours or go mobile.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,The tooling ships fast. That’s good for a workshop.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The vehicle costs are high. A mobile service might be too expensive to run.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,The retired technician is gone. We can’t certify tools without him.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,The equipment budget was under. We have some slack there.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,The mobile service could reach the outer wards. That solves the access issue.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I think the mobile service is the most resilient. It doesn't depend on one building.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. It avoids the digitisation trap.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,I am concerned about the staff. Who will drive the van?,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,We can use the equipment slack to buy the van. The grant covers the sessions.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,Yes. It reaches the people who can't come to us.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
